 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A digital identity is all the information about a person that exists online: usernames, e-mail addresses, profiles and photos on social media, phone numbers, passwords, posts, likes and comments.\nOnline accounts are protected by authentication: a username and a password, a PIN, a fingerprint or face recognition, or a code sent by SMS (two-step verification).\nA strong password is long (at least 8–12 characters) and mixes capital and small letters, numbers and symbols; it is not a name or a birthday, and it is never shared.\nRisks: identity theft (someone pretends to be you), hacked accounts, scams (fake messages asking for codes or mobile money PINs), cyberbullying.\nProtect your identity: strong, different passwords; two-step verification; never share PINs or codes; check privacy settings; think before posting.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
